.TITLE "scp"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Securely copies files between hosts on a network. It uses __SSH__ for data transfer and provides the same level of __encryption__ and security as a remote login.

.DIV "TLDR"
**scp file user@host:path**
Copies a local file to a specific path on a remote server.
> __file__ local source | __user@host:path__ remote destination

**scp user@host:path destination**
Downloads a file from a remote server to a local directory.
> __user@host:path__ remote source | __destination__ local target

**scp -r folder user@host:path**
Recursively copies an entire directory to a remote server.
> __-r__ recursive flag | __folder__ local source | __user@host:path__ remote target

**scp -P port file user@host:path**
Uses a specific port to connect to the remote server.
> __-P__ port flag | __port__ numeric port | __file__ source | __user@host:path__ target

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Note that __scp__ uses an uppercase __-P__ for the port, unlike __ssh__ which uses lowercase. For large or complex transfers that might be interrupted, consider using __rsync__ instead for its ability to resume transfers.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:ssh**

